{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"controlled-ornate-honeybee","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Duplicated local->Jira value maps inside adapters/jira/ have already drifted\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered while authoring J1's characterization oracles for epic e369 (Jira-family seam). The local->Jira\nstatus and priority value maps exist in **two independent copies** within `adapters/jira/`:\n\n- `adapters/jira/jira_fields.py`: `_LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` / `_LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA` — read **only** by the\n  ACLI transport (`acli.py:69-70,143,171`; `acli_cli_ops.py:34,343,354`).\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py`: `_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_STATUS` / `_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_PRIORITY` — read by the\n  `Backend` port (`backend.py`'s `map_fields_to_remote` / `_map_local_to_jira_fields`).\n\n**They have already drifted:** `outbound_fields._LOCAL_TO_JIRA_STATUS` contains a `\"deleted\": \"Done\"` entry\nthat `jira_fields._LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` does not. So a local ticket with status `deleted` maps to `Done`\nthrough the backend port but falls through to the `status.replace(\"_\", \" \").title()` fallback (`\"Deleted\"` —\nnot a live DIG workflow state) through the ACLI path.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFound by a mutation that FAILED to go red: altering `jira_fields._LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA['blocked']` from\n`\"In Progress\"` to `\"To Do\"` left the whole backend characterization suite GREEN (30/30), because no\nbackend-port oracle reaches that copy. The same mutation applied to `outbound_fields._LOCAL_TO_JIRA_STATUS`\nturned 2 tests RED. The ACLI-side copy is effectively unpinned.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nEpic e369's premise is \"no mapping logic in two places\". That duplication is usually framed as Cloud-vs-DC, but\nit **already exists inside the Cloud adapter**, and it is the un-oracled side. Any Jira-family extraction that\nconsolidates only the `outbound_fields` copy will leave the ACLI copy behind and the drift intact.\n\n## Approach\n\nSingle-source the maps in the new `adapters/jira_family/` layer (J2's target) and have BOTH the ACLI transport\nand the `Backend` port read that one definition. Decide explicitly what the correct `deleted` mapping is —\nthe drift means one of the two current behaviors is wrong, so this is a behavior decision, not a pure\nrefactor, and it needs its own oracle rather than being smuggled into J2's behavior-preserving move.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] exactly one definition of the local->Jira status map and one of the priority map is reachable from both\n      the ACLI transport and the Backend port (verified by grep: no second dict literal)\n- [ ] a characterization test pins the ACLI path's status/priority resolution, so a mutation to the shared map\n      turns an ACLI-side test RED (the gap this bug reports)\n- [ ] the `deleted` status behavior is identical through both paths, and a test pins the chosen value\n- [ ] `make test` green","id":"fe15-3bc4-ed70-4b61","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Local->Jira status/priority value maps are duplicated and already drifted inside adapters/jira/"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785288800360575001,"uuid":"0899c145-b02c-4bd1-ae9a-a871a3acbbf1"}